      "kind": "social",
      "title": "Deacon Vey's Confession",
      "prose": "Beneath the temple's cracked bell, Deacon Vey confesses the seal once bound a small spirit that keeps the ward's cisterns from souring during floods. He fears the guild or the manor would sell the water rights and let the binding lapse for profit.",
